---
import Base from '#layouts/Base.astro';
import CaughtCard from '#components/CaughtCard.astro';
import { SITE } from '#lib/site';
import { CASES, REPO_COUNT } from '#lib/caught-in-the-wild';

const locale = 'en';
---

<Base
  title="Caught in the wild · argot"
  description="Five real findings from running argot against 33 open-source repositories' git history — verified, date-stamped, never mocking."
  locale={locale}
>
  <header class="sticky top-0 z-40 border-b border-line bg-bg/80 backdrop-blur-md">
    <div class="mx-auto flex h-16 max-w-5xl items-center justify-between gap-4 px-5">
      <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-2.5" aria-label="argot — home">
        <span class="wordmark text-lg">ar<span class="g">g</span>ot</span>
        <span class="rounded-md border border-line px-2 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs text-muted"
          >caught in the wild</span
        >
      </a>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 sm:gap-3">
        <a
          href="/docs/"
          class="rounded-md px-2 py-1.5 text-sm text-ink-dim transition-colors hover:text-ink"
          >Docs</a
        >
        <a
          href="/fr/caught-in-the-wild/"
          class="rounded-md border border-line px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-medium text-ink-dim uppercase transition-colors hover:border-line-2 hover:text-ink"
          aria-label="Switch to fr">fr</a
        >
        <a
          href={SITE.github}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="rounded-md border border-line bg-panel/60 px-3 py-1.5 text-sm transition-colors hover:border-line-2"
          >GitHub ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Caught in the wild</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-ink-dim text-pretty">
      In July 2026 we ran argot against the last 12 months of history on {REPO_COUNT} real
      open-source repositories — dagster, hono, rich, saleor, faker, and {REPO_COUNT - 5} more —
      and adversarially verified every finding below against the code at HEAD. These aren’t
      synthetic examples: real diffs, real commits, real repos maintained by people who write
      excellent code. That’s the point. Even the best codebases accumulate conventions nobody
      wrote down, and the code that breaks one doesn’t look wrong — it looks like a plausible,
      well-typed, perfectly reasonable PR.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-8">
      {CASES.map((item, index) => <CaughtCard item={item} index={index} locale={locale} />)}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-12 text-sm text-muted text-pretty">
      Methodology: for each case, argot fit at the commit before the change, scored the
      introducing commit cold, and the finding was independently attacked by a reviewer briefed
      to disprove it — every case above survived.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
